orchestrator response is retrievable by query_id.\"\"\"\n        from src.models.schemas import OrchestratorResponseRecord\n        db = DatabaseManager(db_path=tmp_path / \"test.db\")\n        await db.initialize()\n\n        query_id = str(uuid.uuid4())\n        await db.save_query(QueryRecord(query_id=query_id, query_text=\"q\"))\n\n        or_record = OrchestratorResponseRecord(\n            response_id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n            query_id=query_id,\n            summary=\"Acting pay is...\",\n            overall_confidence=\"medium\",\n        )\n        await db.save_orchestrator_response(or_record)\n        result = await db.get_orchestrator_response(query_id)\n        assert result.summary == \"Acting pay is...\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of gaps by priority\n\n| Priority | Module | Gap |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Critical** | `orchestrator.py` | JSON fallback returns wrong confidence; routing fallback never exercised |\n| **Critical** | `specialist.py` | Parse fallback, fetch failures, empty instruments — all dark |\n| **Critical** | `db.py` | 9/11 methods have zero test coverage |\n| **High** | `engine.py` | URL normalisation, stale fallback, `FetchError` contract |\n| **High** | `websocket.py` | Connection lifecycle, send failures, `process_query()` |\n| **Medium** | `cache.py` | TTL routing, `is_valid()`, `clear_expired()` |\n| **Medium** | `base.py` | `build_prompt()` with and without context |\n| **Low** | `extractors.py` | Domain selector matching, truncation, element removal |\n",
